Sval: test_trackingprotection_bug1157081.html opens its second window without the first one's workspace

A window takes a workspace no other window shows and opens that
workspace's tabs (spec §10.7), and closing a window keeps its workspace
once a page was browsed in it. The test's first window
browses its page, so the second window shows that workspace and restores
its tab while the test loads its own. The test hangs its load listener on
whichever page the window shows when a DOMContentLoaded arrives, so the
restore can take that page away and the load never comes. Only
browser-chrome files get SvalTestLeftovers between files, so the test
calls it before its first window, to record the workspaces it starts
with, and again once that window has closed.

